  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "When the three kings inheritance opens and drains immortal essence, the San Cha Mountain blessed land faces destruction risk, and Ba Gui awakens from slumber to find the fated person. Fang Yuan reaches the dark blue bronze hall already after that awakening, notes the land spirit’s jade shell, elephant-like legs, and dragon whiskers, and treats refining second aperture Gu as the ownership test.",
      "chapters": [
        377
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_san_cha_mountain",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "gu_second_aperture_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "It appears as a huge tortoise, large as a house. A thick and hard jade thin shell sits on its back. Its four legs are like elephant legs, and two dragon whiskers grow from its face. It opens wrinkled eyes when Fang Yuan wakes in the bronze hall.",
      "chapters": [
        377
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Three children later called the three kings once used the open blessed land to cultivate, returned after revenge, failed to reach rank six, and before death remodelled the place into the three kings inheritance. Ba Gui watched without stopping them, hoping the inheritance would draw a qualified strength path Gu Master. The fated person had to walk strength path, hold beast phantoms, be strong enough, and be near death. Fang Yuan meets those terms and begins the Immortal Gu refinement with Ba Gui’s help, including the full recipe and transport inside the blessed land.",
      "chapters": [
        377
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "three-kings-and-the-fated-owner",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master",
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ba Gui’s first withering at the end of the first San Cha climax.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "first-withering",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After Fang Yuan succeeds in refining divine travel Gu, the aged land spirit praises him, says it cannot see second aperture Gu finished, and fades until it disappears. Immortal essence can no longer be used through it, and this life gave it a proper death compared with a prior-life death under Gu Master assault.",
      "chapters": [
        394
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "first-withering",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_divine_travel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The restart of the San Cha climax and Ba Gui’s final aid.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "restart-and-exit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later uses Spring Autumn Cicada and returns to an earlier point still inside the blessed land.",
      "chapters": [
        399
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "restart-and-exit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_spring_autumn_cicada"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On the second pass he addresses Ba Gui again, reveals Spring Autumn Cicada’s aura at once, and quickly convinces the land spirit with future knowledge.",
      "chapters": [
        400
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "restart-and-exit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In that pass Ba Gui again aids the refinement, then spends remaining immortal essence to activate Fixed Immortal Travel for Fang Yuan’s escape, saying death is a relief and wishing only that second aperture Gu succeed later. The blessed land collapses as Fang Yuan leaves.",
      "chapters": [
        405
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "restart-and-exit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_fixed_immortal_travel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later land spirit comparison still names Ba Gui from the three kings blessed land as an example of a spirit that could teleport others.",
      "chapters": [
        416
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "restart-and-exit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
